# Line endings
#
# core.autocrlf is false here, so without these rules git stores whatever bytes
# the editor wrote. A tool that rewrites a file as CRLF then shows every single
# line as modified — a 2-line edit to articles_overview.md arrived as a 67-line
# diff. Normalizing on add means those rewrites become no-ops.
#
# Note: ~431 files were committed with CRLF before this file existed. They are
# not rewritten retroactively; each gets a one-time whole-file diff the next
# time it is staged. Run `git add --renormalize .` as its own commit to do them
# all at once instead.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they break in containers.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize or diff these as text.
*.png  binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.db   binary
*.dll  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
